# SafePost Backup — Architectural Rules & Codebase Contract
# Generated from deep audit on 2026-04-17. Based strictly on existing code.
# Last updated: 2026-04-17 (post-refactor v2.2.0 — modular components + ExtensionStorage)
# Any AI agent generating code for this project MUST follow these rules.

---

## 1. Project Identity & Stack

- **Name:** SafePost Backup (`fb-auto-suite` in package.json, version 2.2.0)
- **Purpose:** Automated Facebook Group posting system with scheduling, AI content generation, and analytics.
- **Language:** Hebrew-first product (RTL UI, Hebrew synonyms for spin, Hebrew UX copy). All user-facing strings default to Hebrew unless the feature is English-only (status badges, technical labels).
- **Architecture:** Three-tier — React SPA (Vercel) + Express/Node.js API (Render) + Chrome Extension MV3 (local install).

### Tech Stack — Do NOT introduce alternatives

| Layer | Technology | Notes |
|-------|-----------|-------|
| Frontend | React 18 + Vite 6 | JSX only, no TypeScript in production code |
| Styling | Tailwind CSS 3 + `class-variance-authority` + `tailwind-merge` | Dark/light via `darkMode: 'class'` on `<html>` |
| Icons | `lucide-react` | **NEVER** import from other icon libraries |
| Animation | `framer-motion` | Available but used sparingly |
| UI Primitives | `@radix-ui/react-slot` | Used in `Button` component only |
| Backend | Express 5 (CommonJS `.cjs` files) | Runs on Render |
| Database | Supabase (PostgreSQL + Storage) | Via `@supabase/supabase-js` |
| Real-time | Socket.IO 4 (server↔dashboard) + SSE (server→extension) | Two separate channels |
| AI | Google Gemini (`@google/generative-ai`) primary, Anthropic Claude fallback | Dual-provider with graceful degradation |
| Extension | Chrome MV3 — `service_worker` background, content scripts on `facebook.com` | Manifest V3 only |

---

## 2. File Structure — Canonical Locations

```
server/
  index.cjs              # ALL Express routes, SSE, Socket.IO, queue poller, heartbeat
  supabaseClient.cjs     # Singleton Supabase client (server-side, service_role key)

src/
  App.jsx                # Dashboard root (~400 lines): ApiService class, main App component, state orchestration
  main.jsx               # React entry point
  services/
    bridge.js            # BridgeService — extension↔web message abstraction
  utils/
    timeUtils.js         # formatLocalTime, formatLocalDateTime, getLocalDateTimeInput, toUTCISO
  lib/
    utils.js             # cn() — Tailwind class merger (clsx + twMerge)
  components/
    ErrorBoundary.jsx    # React error boundary — wraps AnalyticsPanel to isolate crashes
    QueueTable.jsx       # Task queue table with selection, status badges, proof links
    StatsBar.jsx         # KPI cards (Total, Pending, Completed, Failed)
    SchedulerForm.jsx    # Single-group post form (legacy, secondary to App.jsx launchpad)
    TaskTimer.jsx        # Live MM:SS countdown per task row
    Toast.jsx            # Auto-dismissing notification (success/error/info)
    modals/
      SaveFolderModal.jsx        # Save selected groups as a folder
      StopWorkerModal.jsx        # Confirm worker stop
      SavePostTemplateModal.jsx  # Save post as template
      AiPostAssistantModal.jsx   # AI chat interface (decoupled via onGenerate prop)
    panels/
      AnalyticsPanel.jsx         # 30-day analytics dashboard with Gauge + DonutChart SVGs
    ui/
      button.jsx         # CVA-based Button with variant/size system
      calendar-bento.jsx # Custom calendar widget
      dock.jsx           # Apple-style dock component
      apple-dock-demo.jsx

safe_post_extension/     # PRODUCTION extension folder
  manifest.json          # MV3 manifest, version 7.2
  background.js          # Service worker: alarm polling, SSE listener, job dispatch, group sync
  extensionStorage.js    # ExtStorage helper — chrome.storage.local wrapper (loaded via importScripts)
  content.js             # Facebook DOM automation: post creation, typing, media upload, HUD
  popup.html             # Extension popup

public/
  scripts/
    bridge.js            # Content script bridge (web↔extension message relay via window.postMessage)
    dashboard-bridge.js  # Zero-config bridge with DOM beacon + CustomEvent protocol
    background.js        # Copy/variant of extension background
    content.js           # Copy/variant of extension content
  manifest.json          # Public copy of manifest
```

### Critical Rules

- **`server/index.cjs` is the single source of truth for ALL backend routes.** Do NOT create separate route files, controllers, or middleware modules. All routes live in this file.
- **`src/App.jsx` is the dashboard root and orchestrator.** It holds the `ApiService` class, global state, and composes extracted components. Modals live in `src/components/modals/`, panels in `src/components/panels/`. When adding new modals/panels, follow this split — do NOT inline them back into App.jsx.
- **Components receive data/callbacks via props** — they never call `ApiService` directly. Example: `AiPostAssistantModal` receives `onGenerate={ApiService.generateAiContent.bind(ApiService)}` instead of importing `ApiService`.
- **`safe_post_extension/` is the production extension.** The `public/scripts/` and `extension/` folders contain copies/variants. When modifying extension logic, edit `safe_post_extension/` first.
- **CommonJS (`.cjs`) for all server files.** The project root is `"type": "module"` but the server uses `require()`. Never mix ESM imports into server files.
- **Extension storage goes through `ExtStorage`** (loaded via `importScripts('extensionStorage.js')` in `background.js`). Do NOT call `chrome.storage.local` directly in background.js.

---

## 3. API Service Layer — The ONLY Way to Call the Backend

### Frontend: `ApiService` class (defined near the top of `src/App.jsx`)

**MANDATORY:** All HTTP calls from React MUST go through `ApiService`. Never use raw `fetch()` in components.

```javascript
// CORRECT — Always use ApiService
const data = await ApiService.getQueue();
const result = await ApiService.createPosts({ group_ids, content, schedule, media_url, ai_spin });

// WRONG — Never do this in components
const res = await fetch(`${API_BASE}/queue`);  // FORBIDDEN
```

#### Complete ApiService Method Registry

| Method | HTTP | Endpoint | Used For |
|--------|------|----------|----------|
| `getGroups()` | GET | `/api/groups` | Fetch all Facebook groups |
| `getQueue()` | GET | `/api/queue` | Fetch task queue with group joins |
| `getSystemStatus()` | GET | `/api/system/status` | Worker status, version, last check-in |
| `getGroupSets()` | GET | `/api/group-sets` | Fetch saved group folders |
| `createPosts(data)` | POST | `/api/posts` | Create new posting tasks (bulk) |
| `deleteTask(id)` | DELETE | `/api/tasks/:id` | Delete single task |
| `bulkDelete(ids)` | POST | `/api/tasks/bulk-delete` | Delete multiple tasks |
| `updateTask(id, data)` | PATCH | `/api/tasks/:id` | Update task fields |
| `cancelTask(id)` | POST | `/api/tasks/:id/cancel` | Cancel single pending task |
| `cancelAllPending()` | POST | `/api/tasks/cancel-all-pending` | Cancel all pending tasks |
| `stopWorker()` | POST | `/api/worker/stop` | Send stop signal to extension |
| `resumeWorker()` | POST | `/api/worker/resume` | Resume worker operations |
| `saveGroupSet(name, ids)` | POST | `/api/group-sets` | Save a group folder |
| `deleteGroupSet(id)` | DELETE | `/api/group-sets/:id` | Delete a group folder |
| `getTemplates()` | GET | `/api/templates` | Fetch post templates |
| `saveTemplate(data)` | POST | `/api/templates` | Save a post template |
| `deleteTemplate(id)` | DELETE | `/api/templates/:id` | Delete a template |
| `uploadFile(file)` | POST | `/api/upload` | Upload media (multipart FormData) |
| `generateAiContent(prompt, history)` | POST | `/api/ai/generate` | AI content generation |
| `getAnalytics()` | GET | `/api/analytics` | 30-day analytics dashboard |

#### Adding a New Endpoint

1. Add the Express route in `server/index.cjs` (follow existing patterns: Supabase query → error check → `res.json()`)
2. Add a static method to `ApiService` class in `src/App.jsx`
3. If it's a mutation, emit the appropriate Socket.IO event (`io.emit('queue_updated')` or `io.emit('data_updated')`)
4. Apply `strictLimiter` to expensive endpoints (uploads, AI), `apiLimiter` is already global on `/api/`

### Backend URL Resolution

```javascript
// src/App.jsx:15-26
const BACKEND_URL = (() => {
    if (import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL) return import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL;
    if (window.location.hostname === 'safepost-backup.vercel.app')
        return 'https://safepost-backup.onrender.com';
    return 'https://safepost-backup.onrender.com'; // Fallback
})();
const API_BASE = `${BACKEND_URL}/api`;
```

**Extension uses hardcoded:** `const BASE_URL = 'https://safepost-backup.onrender.com';` in `safe_post_extension/background.js:4`

---

## 4. Real-Time Communication — Two Channels

### Channel 1: Socket.IO (Server ↔ Dashboard)

**Connection:** `src/App.jsx:29-35` — global `socket` instance, auto-reconnect with exponential backoff.

**Events the server emits:**

| Event | Trigger | Dashboard Action |
|-------|---------|-----------------|
| `status_update` | Task status change | Update queue row in-place, record timestamp |
| `queue_updated` | Any queue mutation | Triggers `fetchAllData(true)` (silent refresh) |
| `data_updated` | Group sync complete | Triggers `fetchAllData(true)` |
| `groups_updated` | Groups upserted | Refresh group list |
| `groups_sync_failed` | Sync error | Stop sync spinner, show error |
| `worker_stop_signal` | Stop command sent | Update UI state |
| `worker_resumed` | Resume command sent | Update UI state |

**Pattern — listen in `useEffect`, cleanup on unmount:**
```javascript
useEffect(() => {
    socket.on('queue_updated', () => fetchAllData(true));
    socket.on('status_update', ({ taskId, status }) => { /* update state */ });
    return () => { socket.off('queue_updated'); socket.off('status_update'); };
}, [fetchAllData]);
```

### Channel 2: SSE (Server → Extension)

**Endpoint:** `GET /api/stream/jobs` — server pushes events to connected extensions.

**Events:**

| SSE Type | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `connected` | Handshake confirmation |
| `new_job` | Dispatch a task to the extension worker |
| `sync_groups` | Request extension to scrape Facebook groups |
| `stop_worker` | Tell extension to halt |

**Server broadcast helper:** `broadcastSSE(data)` in `server/index.cjs:245-247`

### Channel 3: Extension ↔ Web App (BridgeService)

**File:** `src/services/bridge.js` — `BridgeService` singleton object.

**Protocol:**
- **Extension mode** (`chrome.runtime.id` exists): Direct `chrome.runtime.sendMessage` / `chrome.runtime.onMessage`
- **Web mode**: `window.postMessage` with protocol markers:
  - Web → Extension: `{ target: 'EXTENSION_BG', action, payload }`
  - Extension → Web: `{ target: 'DASHBOARD_APP', type, data }`

**Content script bridges** (`public/scripts/bridge.js`, `public/scripts/dashboard-bridge.js`):
- `bridge.js`: Relays between `window.postMessage` and `chrome.runtime.sendMessage`
- `dashboard-bridge.js`: Injects DOM beacon (`#safepost-bridge-signal`) + uses `CustomEvent` protocol (`SAFEPOST_REQ` / `SAFEPOST_RES`)

**Extension Message Actions (background.js listener):**

| Action | Direction | Handler |
|--------|-----------|---------|
| `EXECUTE_POST` | BG → Content | Trigger Facebook posting automation |
| `JOB_COMPLETE` | Content → BG | Mark task SUCCESS, close tab |
| `CLOSE_TAB` | Content → BG | Close the Facebook tab |
| `MISSION_FAILED` | Content → BG | Mark task FAILED, close tab |
| `SYNC_GROUPS` | Content → BG | Forward scraped groups to server |
| `REPORT_STATUS` | Content → BG → Server | Log or update task status via PATCH `/api/tasks/:id/status` |
| `GET_COOKIES` | Any → BG | Retrieve Facebook cookies |
| `START_AUTOMATION` | External → BG | Start posting from dashboard (via `externally_connectable`) |
| `SCAN_AND_SYNC_GROUPS` | External → BG | Trigger group scan from dashboard |

---

## 5. Database Schema (Supabase Tables)

Inferred from queries in `server/index.cjs`:

| Table | Key Columns | Notes |
|-------|-------------|-------|
| `posts` | `id`, `group_id`, `content`, `media_url`, `media_paths`, `status`, `scheduled_time`, `app_source`, `failure_reason`, `proof_url`, `created_at`, `ended_at` | `app_source = 'backup'` filter is MANDATORY on all queries |
| `groups` | `id`, `name`, `url` | Facebook group registry, upserted on sync |
| `group_sets` | `id`, `name`, `group_ids` (array), `created_at` | Saved group folders |
| `post_templates` | `id`, `name`, `content`, `media_url`, `app_source`, `created_at` | Reusable post templates |
| `system_logs` | `id`, `log_level`, `source`, `message` | Audit trail for automation events |
| `app_config` | `config_key`, `config_data` (JSONB), `updated_at` | Dynamic extension DOM selectors |

### Critical Supabase Rules

1. **Always filter by `app_source = 'backup'`** when querying `posts`. This table is shared with other apps.
2. **The `posts` table has NO `updated_at` column.** Never include it in updates.
3. **Status lifecycle:** `PENDING` → `SENT` → `PROCESSING` → `SUCCESS` / `FAILED` / `CANCELLED`
4. **Server uses `supabaseClient.cjs`** which prefers `SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY` (RLS bypass). Never expose this key to the frontend.
5. **Storage bucket:** `campaign-media` for all uploaded files.

---

## 6. State Management — React Conventions

### Pattern: `useState` + `useCallback` + Socket.IO events

There is **no Redux, Zustand, or Context API** in this project. All state lives in `App()` via `useState` hooks.

**Core state variables (App.jsx):**

| State | Type | Purpose |
|-------|------|---------|
| `groups` | `Group[]` | All Facebook groups from Supabase |
| `queue` | `Task[]` | All tasks (posts) in the queue |
| `serverStatus` | `boolean` | Server reachable (3 consecutive failures = offline) |
| `workerStatus` | `{ status, message, last_checkin }` | Extension worker health |
| `selectedGroups` | `string[]` | Group IDs selected for posting |
| `postContent` | `string` | Current post text |
| `scheduleTime` | `string` | Datetime-local string for scheduling |
| `theme` | `'dark' \| 'light'` | Persisted in `localStorage` |
| `selectedTaskIds` | `string[]` | Selected task IDs in queue table |
| `statusTimestamps` | `{ [taskId]: { [status]: timeString } }` | Timeline of status transitions |

**Data refresh pattern:**

```javascript
const fetchAllData = useCallback(async (silent = false) => {
    if (!silent) setLoading(true);
    const [gData, qData, sData, gsData, tData] = await Promise.all([
        ApiService.getGroups(), ApiService.getQueue(),
        ApiService.getSystemStatus(), ApiService.getGroupSets(),
        ApiService.getTemplates()
    ]);
    // ... set all state ...
}, []);
```

**ALWAYS use `fetchAllData(true)` for silent refreshes** (no loading spinner). Socket.IO events trigger silent refreshes.

